{"title":"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a rectangle with sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/0/d60fd1af68d4091b9ac24a71589e62f963dba074.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB&gt;BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/f/c8f799905273ed1464a723a84b80addec5334bc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC=AD$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> and the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/e/1ce64e131c6a3564a33b255b02312704b2c03860.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ECBD$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50ff9540650f0f95f80da2f6692fc8ee413e2eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/1/801ebac08197a6cd9bcc0e32a77b04e3a73793a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD = 90$\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" /> degrees, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/a/b8a785e2421ca96626c0264e05abd38281e0c461.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BED = 90$\" width=\"99\" height=\"12\" /> degrees. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the circle with diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />, or the circumcircle of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. We are given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8f18339a31972228e007e5d3e22ffc40137b4f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC=BC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"12\" />, so by symmetry, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/7/e47d5c58ed0e56aedd92d5a0e520710c865cc9b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC=ED$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" />. Since the three lengths are equal and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/b/12b1ca22ba68cef9c309850e3014344f10424c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overarc{BD}=180$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> degrees, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/6/6969d644d0b93027b8f860870cc239302569a0c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overarc{BC}=\\overarc{CE}=\\overarc{ED}=60$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" /> degrees, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/2/f820b345347a6b0b992f9441716d66c2a6bdf5bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OBC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/2/852fac5dd9068681f6e27e3684cb352297ae79ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OCE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f602b96698902da755a62d059f61424bbeaf68e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OED$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> are all equilateral. Given that the area of cyclic quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/e/1ce64e131c6a3564a33b255b02312704b2c03860.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ECBD$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50ff9540650f0f95f80da2f6692fc8ee413e2eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/2/f820b345347a6b0b992f9441716d66c2a6bdf5bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OBC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43f0f23f45710d6ca85de3b530f5a5dc9ddef7f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 144 = 48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"95\" height=\"37\" />. This is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the area of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/5/93565df93309c1634a2831ce175c2f10189599a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48 \\cdot 4 = \\boxed{192}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I\" title=\"2020 CIME I\">2020 CIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 CIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2020\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"CIME Problems and Solutions\"> All CIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:MAC_Notice&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:MAC Notice (page does not exist)\">Template:MAC Notice</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018013001\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.076 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 243/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1870/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5519/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   28.998      1 -total\n 50.98%   14.783      1 Template:Image\n 27.18%    7.882      1 Template:CIME_box\n  8.04%    2.331      1 Template:MAC_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with ke